2|The Five-Minute Morning|只剩五分钟的早晨|家庭日常|快迟到了，Lucy却找不到自己的鞋；一家人分头寻找。|催促、寻找物品、确认时间
ready=准备好的|by the door=在门边|matching=成对的
Has anyone seen my other shoe?|We've got five minutes.|I'm ready now.
lucy: Little Moments. The Five-Minute Morning. My alarm rings, and I turn it off. I close my eyes for just a second. When I open them again, Mom is standing in my doorway with my backpack.
mom: Good morning, sleepyhead. We've got five minutes. Your breakfast is on the table.
lucy: Five minutes? That can't be right. I jump out of bed, pull on my clothes, and discover a problem. Has anyone seen my other shoe?
ben: Which one? The left one or the one you're standing on?
lucy: I look down. One foot is already wearing a sneaker. Very funny. I need the other one. It's white, and it usually lives next to this one.
mom: Check by the door. You took them off there yesterday.
lucy: I find Dad's boots, Ben's sandals, and one tennis ball. No white sneaker. Then I hear a small voice from the living room.
ben: Found it! My stuffed bear was using it as a boat.
lucy: Of course he was. I put it on and race to the kitchen. Mom hands me a banana and a sandwich wrapped in paper.
mom: Breakfast to go today. Tomorrow, let's put everything by the door before bed.
lucy: I'm ready now. Wait. Where's my backpack?
ben: On your back, Captain.
lucy: I reach behind me. He's right again. We make it outside with matching shoes, breakfast, and one whole minute to spare. Tonight, I'm checking my bag before I go to sleep. I'm also hiding my shoes from that bear.
===
3|The Lunchbox Mix-Up|拿错的午餐盒|校园生活|午饭时间打开盒子，Lucy发现自己拿了爸爸的午餐。|说明拿错、分享食物、提出替代办法
lunchbox=午餐盒|mix-up=弄混|trade=交换
I think I grabbed the wrong one.|Would you like half?|Let's check the labels tomorrow.
lucy: Little Moments. The Lunchbox Mix-Up. At lunch, Emma sits across from me and opens her sandwich. I open my blue lunchbox, expecting pasta. Inside, I find a giant salad, a small jar of dressing, and a note that says, Have a great meeting.
emma: Wow. Is your sandwich hiding under all that lettuce?
lucy: I think I grabbed the wrong one. Dad and I have exactly the same lunchbox. Mine was supposed to have pasta and apple slices.
emma: So your dad is going to a meeting with apple slices and a dinosaur fork?
lucy: I picture him opening the box. Actually, he probably likes the dinosaur fork. I send Mom a message through the school office, just so nobody worries.
emma: I have an extra bread roll. Would you like half?
lucy: Thanks. I have plenty of cucumber if you want some. We check that the food is okay for both of us, then put a clean napkin between our lunches.
emma: Look at us. We accidentally opened a tiny restaurant.
lucy: That afternoon, Dad is waiting at home with both empty lunchboxes. He holds up the dinosaur fork like a prize.
dad: Excellent pasta. Very professional fork. How was my salad?
lucy: Crunchy. Really crunchy. Let's check the labels tomorrow.
dad: Good idea. Mine can say Dad, and yours can say Lucy.
lucy: Ben suggests a third label for himself: Person Who Would Like More Pasta. We give him a sticker, but we keep our lunchboxes.
===
4|Is This Seat Taken?|这里有人坐吗|校园生活|Lucy在图书馆找座位，和Emma一起寻找一本有趣的书。|询问空位、借书、表达阅读偏好
seat=座位|due=到期的|shelf=书架
Is this seat taken?|I'm looking for something funny.|When is it due?
lucy: Little Moments. Is This Seat Taken? The school library is busy after lunch. I carry two heavy books between the tables until I spot Emma beside an empty chair. Is this seat taken?
emma: It's yours. Just watch out for my backpack. It's trying to take over the floor.
lucy: I sit down and put my books on the table. One is about mountain climbing. The other is about a detective who loses his own keys. I'm looking for something funny.
emma: Then I'd start with the detective. Losing your keys while solving a mystery sounds pretty good.
lucy: I open the first page. The detective is locked outside his office. Emma leans over, and we both start laughing. We quickly cover our mouths because everyone else is reading quietly.
staff: Sounds like you found a good one. Would you like to check it out?
lucy: Yes, please. When is it due?
staff: In two weeks. The date is on this slip. You can renew it if nobody else is waiting for it.
emma: Can I borrow it after you? No spoilers, though.
lucy: Deal. I put the library slip inside the book and check my pockets before we leave.
emma: What are you looking for?
lucy: My house key. I don't want to end up like this detective.
staff: A very sensible decision.
lucy: My key is exactly where it belongs. The detective would be impressed. Now he just needs to find his.
===
5|A Cart With One Wobbly Wheel|购物车的小麻烦|吃饭与购物|Lucy和妈妈按清单购物，Ben一直试图加入新东西。|寻找货架、核对清单、比较包装
cart=购物车|aisle=货架通道|list=清单
Which aisle is the cereal in?|Is that on the list?|We already have some at home.
lucy: Little Moments. A Cart With One Wobbly Wheel. Our shopping cart makes a tiny squeak every time Mom turns a corner. Ben thinks it sounds like a mouse. I think it sounds like a mouse asking for a vacation.
mom: We need milk, eggs, bread, and cereal. Lucy, can you hold the list?
ben: And cookies. Very important cookies.
lucy: Is that on the list? Ben looks over my shoulder as if the word might appear if he stares hard enough. It doesn't. We reach the end of the aisle, but there's still no cereal.
mom: Excuse me. Which aisle is the cereal in?
clerk: Aisle five, next to the oatmeal. The signs above you show the aisle numbers.
lucy: Thanks. In aisle five, Ben picks up the biggest box he can reach. It's almost the size of his backpack.
ben: This one has a spaceship on it.
mom: Let's compare the smaller box, too. We only need enough for this week, and we already have some at home.
lucy: We choose the smaller box and cross cereal off the list. At checkout, I count four things. Milk, eggs, bread, and cereal. Perfect.
ben: The cart did all that work without getting any cookies.
mom: The cart doesn't eat cookies.
ben: That explains the squeaking. It's upset.
lucy: We park it with the other carts. I give it a little wave. Thanks for the ride, tiny mouse. Enjoy your break.
===
6|No Ice, Please|饮料里不要冰|吃饭与购物|一次饮品点单里，Lucy练习清楚说明自己的选择。|点饮料、确认大小、礼貌纠正
lemonade=柠檬水|regular=普通大小的|receipt=小票
Could I get a small lemonade?|No ice, please.|Sorry, I asked for no ice.
lucy: Little Moments. No Ice, Please. Emma and I stop at a little sandwich shop after school. It's warm outside, and we both want something to drink. The menu has about twenty choices. My brain wants all twenty.
emma: I'm getting water. You can study the menu, but I'm not waiting until tomorrow.
lucy: Okay, decision made. Could I get a small lemonade?
clerk: Sure. Regular or strawberry?
lucy: Regular, please. And no ice, please.
clerk: One small regular lemonade with no ice. Anything else?
emma: A cup of water for me, please.
lucy: We move to the end of the counter. A few minutes later, the clerk puts two cups in front of us. My lemonade makes a loud, icy rattle. I glance at Emma.
emma: You can just tell her. She probably has about ten orders in her head.
lucy: Sorry, I asked for no ice.
clerk: Oh, you're right. Thanks for letting me know. I'll make you another one.
lucy: Thank you. I was worried that saying something would feel awkward, but the clerk is already smiling at the next customer. Soon, my new drink is ready.
emma: Better?
lucy: Much better. We sit by the window, and I take a sip. Now I only have one problem.
emma: What is it?
lucy: I still want to know what strawberry lemonade tastes like.
emma: That sounds like a problem for another afternoon.
===
7|The Last Slice|最后一块披萨|家庭日常|一块披萨引发争论，姐弟俩决定公平分配。|表达想要、轮流、商量分配
slice=一块披萨|fair=公平的|split=分开
Are you going to eat that?|Let's split it.|You cut, and I'll choose.
lucy: Little Moments. The Last Slice. Movie night is about to start. There are blankets on the couch, drinks on the table, and exactly one slice of pizza left in the box. Ben and I notice it at the same time.
ben: Are you going to eat that?
lucy: I was thinking about it. Were you?
ben: I've been thinking about it for a very long time. Since the last slice I ate.
dad: Sounds serious. How are you two going to solve this?
lucy: We could race for it. Dad raises one eyebrow. Okay, maybe not. Let's split it.
ben: But one side has more cheese. And one side has the big mushroom.
lucy: You don't even like mushrooms.
ben: I might start tonight.
dad: Here's an idea. One person cuts, and the other person chooses a piece.
lucy: You cut, and I'll choose. Ben studies the pizza like it's a very important map. Dad helps him use the pizza cutter, and we look at the two pieces.
ben: They're almost the same. Except this one has a tiny extra corner.
lucy: I choose the other piece. Ben looks surprised, then takes the corner with a smile. We sit down just as the movie starts.
dad: Everybody happy?
ben: Very happy. Next time, though, could we order one more pizza?
lucy: Dad laughs. I take a bite and discover the big mushroom on my piece. Apparently, Ben has decided not to start liking mushrooms tonight after all.
===
8|Wait, That's My Hoodie|等等，那是我的卫衣|家庭日常|Lucy想穿的卫衣不见了，原来Ben把它当成了自己的新衣服。|描述衣物、请求借用、约定归还
hoodie=连帽卫衣|sleeve=袖子|borrow=借用
Can I borrow it?|It looks a little big on you.|Please ask me first next time.
lucy: Little Moments. Wait, That's My Hoodie. I'm getting ready to meet Emma when I notice something missing. My favorite green hoodie isn't on my chair. It isn't in my closet, either. Then a small green shape walks past my door.
ben: Morning. Nice weather, right?
lucy: Wait, that's my hoodie. Ben stops. The sleeves cover both his hands, and the bottom reaches almost to his knees. It looks a little big on you.
ben: That's the style. Very comfortable. Lots of room for snacks.
lucy: I was going to wear it today. Did you take it from my chair?
ben: Maybe. Can I borrow it?
lucy: You're supposed to ask that before you put it on.
mom: Everything okay in here?
lucy: We're having a small fashion discussion. I need my hoodie, and Ben seems to be living inside it.
ben: I like the big pocket. My own sweatshirt doesn't have one.
mom: Your blue jacket has two pockets. It's hanging by the door.
ben: Two pockets? That does change things.
lucy: He pulls off the hoodie and hands it back. I check the pocket and find a toy car, a clean tissue, and a tiny rubber duck. Please ask me first next time.
ben: Deal. Can I borrow it tomorrow?
lucy: Maybe. Ask me tomorrow. For now, your duck needs a new apartment.
ben: The blue jacket has room. He can have his own pocket.
===
9|The Bus Going the Other Way|公交车方向坐反了？|出行与办事|Lucy和爸爸在上车前发现站错方向，及时换到马路对面。|问方向、确认站点、询问车程
across the street=在街道对面|stop=站点|direction=方向
Does this bus go to the museum?|You're on the wrong side of the street.|How many stops is it?
lucy: Little Moments. The Bus Going the Other Way. Dad and I are taking the bus to the museum. We find a stop with the right number and wait under the sign. I feel very proud of my excellent planning.
dad: Did you check which direction it's going?
lucy: Same number, same bus. Isn't that enough? Dad points across the street. There's another stop with the same number. Before I can answer, a bus pulls up.
staff: Morning. Where are you headed?
lucy: Does this bus go to the museum?
staff: It does on the way back, but you're on the wrong side of the street. You want the stop across from this one.
dad: Thanks for checking. We'll cross at the lights.
lucy: We wait for the crossing signal and walk to the other stop. The little route map shows the museum four stops away. My excellent planning needs a small update.
dad: Good thing we asked before we sat down.
lucy: When the next bus arrives, I ask the driver again. This time, she says yes. How many stops is it?
clerk: Four from here. I'll call out the museum stop, too.
lucy: Thank you. We sit near the middle, and I watch the names appear on the screen.
dad: Still our chief trip planner?
lucy: Absolutely. I've just added a new rule to my system. Check the number, check the direction, and don't act like a genius until you're on the right bus.
